.TH "PB-PREVIEW-DELETE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-preview-delete - Delete a temporary preview


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb preview delete <preview> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Delete a temporary preview

.PP
End the selected temporary preview and its published access. This command currently performs the same stop operation as pb preview stop; use status first if you need its current state.

.PP
A preview exposes a local target through a temporary Paperboat URL or private/team access policy. Inspect its status before sharing the URL, and stop or delete it when no longer needed. Browser HTTP terminates TLS at the edge.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for delete

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print the deleted canonical preview resource as JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-preview(1)\fP
